<!--
MFE Fighter — inertia tensor and collision geometry, derived virtually (07/10/2026)
Battery scenario: 2x Tattu 30C 16000mAh 6S (ACTIVE / used for the simulator)
  Alternative (2x ARES 22000mAh 6S Li-ion) computed too: ixx=2.6172 iyy=0.9269 izz=3.4594
  ixy=-0.00007 ixz=0.00001 iyz=0.1266 — within 0.2% of the Tattu values below in every
  component, so the battery choice does not meaningfully affect inertia either way.
Axes: X = wingspan (lateral), Y = fuselage length (+Y = nose), Z = height
Origin: this inertial/collision block assumes the link origin is placed at the CG
        (X=0, Y=+40.997mm from the model's own CAD reference, Z=0)

Mass reconciliation note: total mass below sums to 10.0kg (MTOW 11.5kg minus 1.5kg payload).
The airframe-only portion (4.179kg) is ~1.48kg heavier than the manual's stated 2.7kg
"net weight" — likely wiring, fasteners, adhesive, and any reinforcement not itemised
elsewhere. Not yet resolved; revisit once the real aircraft can be weighed.

Collision geometry is a 6-box primitive approximation (fuselage, 2 booms, 2 wings,
1 combined tail assembly), sized from the verified CAD model's own bounding boxes —
standard practice for flight-dynamics sims, far cheaper than full mesh collision.
-->

<inertial>
  <pose>0 0.040997 0 0 0 0</pose>  <!-- CG offset from model origin, metres -->
  <mass>10.0</mass>
  <inertia>
    <ixx>2.6204</ixx>
    <iyy>0.9287</iyy>
    <izz>3.4642</izz>
    <ixy>-0.00007</ixy>
    <ixz>0.00001</ixz>
    <iyz>0.1269</iyz>
  </inertia>
</inertial>

<!-- Collision geometry: 6 primitive boxes, poses given relative to the model's own
     CAD origin (NOT relative to the CG above) — adjust if your link origin differs -->

